{
  "dom_id": "step-e5206",
  "name": "Example: Dividing Rational Expressions with No Common Factors",
  "problem": "What is the result of dividing $\\dfrac 3 x$ by $\\dfrac {5}{y}?$",
  "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{x} \\div \\dfrac{5}{y},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac 3 x \\div  \\dfrac 5 y&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac 3 x \\cdot  \\dfrac y 5&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {3y} {5x}\t\t\n\t}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
